Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract ", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97889635012245*^9, 3.978896351879611*^9}, 
   3.979349058650394*^9},ExpressionUUID->"01d70810-8ee9-4c00-848e-\
4511290397ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook extends the Relativity Toolkit into Non-Abelian Gauge Theory, \
specifically into Yang-Mills theory. Building on previous machinery for \
Abelian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "3dc32ce2-5543-49b4-93e9-c421a8fec1ad"],
 " electrodynamics, we now tackle non-Abelian symmetries, where the order of \
operations matters\[LongDash]where rotating by \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "79382ad9-5b2a-49f3-9044-5b4997cd0325"],
 " then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["B", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "06a9e9e1-3995-4b62-867b-75ed3d2ae662"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is different from \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["B", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8cd6b401-e364-437a-98a0-84fd9862b1fa"],
 " then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "aad83b65-55b3-4c0f-a6d8-8ff0ea70fc74"],
 ".\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Non-commutative rotations should be familiar from \
ordinary 3D space rotation, where the symmetry group is SO(3). "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980093982951066*^9, 
  3.9800941851238623`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3e91d720-51f9-4ada-b7d5-\
5a723a2e4c70"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this notebook, we implement the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] \
machinery for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"SU", 
    RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d76acf3e-7d52-40b6-b89f-c9454e4c6c9e"],
 " isospin symmetry, introducing a generalized Covariant Derivative that \
handles matrix-valued fields and non-commutative generators. This is achieved \
via Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s NonCommutativeMultiply (**) operator, without \
breaking existing functionality . All previous General Relativity and \
Gauge-Theory notebooks remain valid."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980093982951066*^9, 3.9800940367954273`*^9}, {
  3.980094199364449*^9, 
  3.9800942854859953`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"014435af-88c8-4fd7-9159-\
c6c6c52e94ad"],

Cell["\<\
This work is the first in a multi-part series aiming to derive the full \
Standard Model from first principles. Along the way, we use interactive \
Manipulate visualizations to build intuition for these abstract internal \
spaces, and we frequently surface Noether\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Theorem as our \
primary guide: every new symmetry we encode into \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] reveals a corresponding conservation law, serving as a \
chain of navigational buoys across the vast ocean of the Standard Model of \
particle physics.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980093982951066*^9, 3.9800940367954273`*^9}, {
  3.980094199364449*^9, 
  3.9800943556429977`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ce4fa437-b070-4f11-99fe-\
f9e50bd82ebb"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094562245645*^9, 
  3.980094563916959*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"99b95f0d-6e81-4743-8c2f-\
11b7663afbd9"],

Cell["### 1. The Non-Abelian Leap", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094601300047*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3d5535a3-5e2d-416a-a0e1-\
084b3b753d10"],

Cell["\<\
In our previous notebook, *Non-Quantum Gauge Theory*, we discovered that \
Electrodynamics is effectively the geometry of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]local \
phase\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. We treated the vector potential  as a \
connection\[LongDash]a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]garbage collector\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] that cancels out the artifacts of differentiating a \
field whose phase changes from point to point. That theory was **Abelian**: \
it didn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t matter in which order we applied phase shifts, \
because complex numbers commute ().\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.9800946028042097`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fd41b3d1-862d-4b82-bcd9-\
19427025bcce"],

Cell["\<\
Now, we take the decisive leap into **Non-Abelian** territory. We replace the \
simple circle of phase () with more complex internal shapes, like the \
3-sphere of  . In these spaces, rotations do *not* commute. This seemingly \
small mathematical difference has profound physical consequences:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094603997838*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1862e5fe-3056-4201-81df-\
7e1c0441fa1b"],

Cell["\<\
* **Self-Interaction:** Unlike photons, which pass through each other, the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]force carriers\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of non-Abelian \
theories (like gluons or W bosons) carry charge themselves. They interact \
with *each other*.
* **Non-Linearity:** The field strength tensor  acquires a quadratic term (), \
making the equations of motion inherently non-linear and fascinatingly \
complex.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094605163763*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1e70cc90-c160-41fa-b036-\
081ee590f124"],

Cell["### 2. The Roadmap: To the Standard Model", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.9800946062779617`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f33a52e4-97ab-460f-9f5b-\
bc3511d81bbe"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook is the foundation for a complete derivation of the Standard \
Model using the UD Calculus. Our planned trajectory is:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.9800946072025023`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b45a0993-24f4-4063-a5ea-\
a804547b76d9"],

Cell["\<\
1. **Non-Abelian Gauge Theory (This Notebook):** Establishing the `**` \
algebra, defining the Yang-Mills field strength, and proving  covariance.
2. **Electroweak Theory (GWS):** Unifying  and  to create the  boson and the \
photon via the Weinberg Angle.
3. **The Higgs Mechanism:** Breaking the symmetry spontaneously to generate \
mass terms.
4. **QCD and the Standard Model:** Adding the  color layer to complete the \
picture.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094608672147*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1a7b9593-974b-4d73-9df5-\
80179241e537"],

Cell["### 3. Software Architecture: The \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Do No Harm\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Principle", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094609507545*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bd7bf4ba-582c-45a2-9ae3-\
119ad00dd0fd"],

Cell["\<\
A major technical objective of this series is to upgrade the **Relativity \
Toolkit** without breaking the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Gold Standard\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] regression tests established in previous works.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.9800946111101513`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d9901220-13eb-47c3-ac77-\
d0915c5ec491"],

Cell["\<\
To achieve this, we have chosen a software architecture that is **additive**, \
not destructive:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094612117598*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d4bc9cbb-e972-4bf6-ad5b-\
df1b09ec2dc8"],

Cell["\<\
* **Separation of Algebra:** We continue to use standard multiplication \
(`Times`, `*`) for scalars and geometric tensors. We introduce \
`NonCommutativeMultiply` (`**`) exclusively for Lie Algebra generators (). \
This prevents the new quantum algebra from interfering with the existing \
General Relativity engine.
* **Overloaded Operators:** The `CD` (Covariant Derivative) operator has been \
upgraded to be \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]variadic.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] It \
can now accept a list of multiple simultaneous gauge corrections (e.g., \
Isospin and Hypercharge) without altering its original behavior for simple \
gravity or electromagnetism.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.9800946139808407`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"221458c5-60d3-41ab-a2c3-\
b39ad3b5d298"],

Cell["\<\
* **Data, Not Code:** We reuse the powerful contraction engine \
(`ContractAll`) by simply passing it different lists of \
indices\[LongDash]swapping spacetime coordinates  for internal color indices \
\[LongDash]allowing us to reuse the robust, debugged core of the toolkit.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094617629334*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d6bdcff9-c557-41a7-a6c0-\
e297bd9f2366"],

Cell["### 4. Noether\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Buoys", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094618663774*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"68586465-b978-4f5e-864d-\
0387cff4bd55"],

Cell["\<\
As we venture into these abstract internal spaces, it is easy to lose sight \
of the physics amidst the sea of indices. To keep us oriented, we will rely \
on **Noether\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Theorem**.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094619702149*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bcf424ee-3731-464c-ad92-\
dbac37c10fe3"],

Cell["In every section, we will look for the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Noether \
Buoy\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094620611465*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6fbc817a-6f05-471a-bdf5-\
50a0c3e85bf3"],

Cell["\<\
* If we construct a Lagrangian invariant under rotation in Isospin space, \
*what is conserved*? (Isospin Current).
* If the field strength is invariant, *what does that imply* for the dynamics \
of the bosons?\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094621967523*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5da9b4ac-ecce-4819-88ef-\
1c7eede39c5e"],

Cell["\<\
We will also use `Manipulate` to visualize these symmetries. It is one thing \
to say \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]invariant under  rotation\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]; it is another to drag a slider and watch a vector \
rotate on a sphere while its energy density remains perfectly still.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.980094623322789*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"311f6dca-3b27-45e3-a043-\
dcc56a13cb25"],

Cell["\<\
Let us begin by defining the algebra of our new internal space.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980094575754602*^9, 
  3.9800946154404287`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bfd265c2-2269-4836-a2ab-\
9787b658a22f"]
}, Open  ]],

