Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["All Physics is Gauge Theory", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978638647735394*^9, 3.9786386508345337`*^9}, {
  3.978641316636702*^9, 3.978641319674756*^9}, {3.978737839482726*^9, 
  3.9787378449477777`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7c1aaaaf-5aaa-4d52-a80b-\
964e26b46f48"],

Cell["Look at the dictionary definition of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge:\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978883652791445*^9, 3.978883667079052*^9}, {
  3.978883709767684*^9, 3.978883717690165*^9}, {3.978890707784769*^9, 
  3.978890709641519*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ce0c3612-3663-4035-a3a8-\
6816239fabad"],

Cell["\<\
n. A device or instrument for measuring the magnitude, amount, or contents of \
something. Ex.: a fuel gauge\
\>", "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978883730048634*^9, 3.978883776510605*^9}, {
  3.978883815692973*^9, 3.978883825839571*^9}, {3.9789931611766644`*^9, 
  3.9789931647744293`*^9}},
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"36ad7096-221b-4ea0-a168-2660e497ea99"],

Cell["\<\
n. The thickness, size, or capacity of something, especially as a standard. \
Ex.: the gauge of a rail line.\
\>", "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978883786455063*^9, 3.9788838086393337`*^9}, {
   3.978883844767459*^9, 3.978883845135405*^9}, {3.9788838779900837`*^9, 
   3.978883887480989*^9}, 3.978993178665461*^9},
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"5cd38cff-9548-46ee-b53d-bf44f5959731"],

Cell["\<\
v. To estimate or determine the magnitude, amount, or volume of something. \
Ex. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Gauge the intrinsic luminosity of a star.\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\
\>", "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788838915047092`*^9, 3.9788839421842003`*^9}, {
  3.978890732797731*^9, 3.978890733962523*^9}, {3.978993189915084*^9, 
  3.978993196958743*^9}},
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"2797d472-d273-422c-9d7f-058ac3138f2b"],

Cell["\<\
v. To measure the dimensions of an object with a gauge instrument. Ex. \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Gauge the assemblies and plane them to width.\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\
\>", "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978883959825788*^9, 3.978884029111815*^9}, {
  3.9788907482661743`*^9, 3.978890760161418*^9}, {3.978993206062478*^9, 
  3.9789932096595297`*^9}},
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"c91721c1-c1e6-464c-950c-7de4968e7b4f"],

Cell["\<\
All this is refreshingly concrete, referring to ordinary objects and \
activities in the trades or in the physics lab. None of it hints at the \
abstractions of gauge theory for electrodynamics, the nuclear forces, \
gravitation, let alone quantum field theory. Where are covariance, \
invariance, symmetry groups, conservation, unitarity, fibre bundles, and so \
on, in these definitions? \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978883959825788*^9, 3.9788843549050817`*^9}, {
  3.978884709404888*^9, 3.978884710636094*^9}, {3.978890785955967*^9, 
  3.978890786256155*^9}, {3.978993226174899*^9, 3.9789932692510433`*^9}, {
  3.97934392409107*^9, 
  3.979343949612047*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"076e2e2d-bcf1-42f8-a1fc-\
ed2dda3a6ea2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The answer is the other way around: all these abstractions are not \
definitional, they\[CloseCurlyQuote]re just mathematical machinery for \
various kinds of gauging, in the sense of measuring various quantities. \
Physics is, fundamentally, the science of measurement, and we can\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t measure anything without setting up gauges. Most \
familiarly, we choose coordinates for measuring positions and momenta in \
spacetime. ",
 StyleBox["Setting a gauge",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is setting coordinate origins and bases for measurements. Likewise, we \
must choose a reference for measuring the phase of an electromagnetic field. ",
 StyleBox["Setting a gauge",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for electrodynamics is setting a phase reference at each point of \
spacetime. By analogy to position and momentum, we can say that setting the \
phase reference is ",
 StyleBox["setting a coordinate system basis and origin for phase",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978884356699004*^9, 3.978884491775428*^9}, {
  3.9788845347619467`*^9, 3.978884683462042*^9}, {3.978884806945133*^9, 
  3.978885107805743*^9}, {3.9788851804396267`*^9, 3.978885192184779*^9}, {
  3.978885388709526*^9, 3.978885417081642*^9}, {3.97888545395669*^9, 
  3.9788854714725657`*^9}, {3.978890798743556*^9, 3.978890932357812*^9}, {
  3.9789933012971067`*^9, 3.978993341347312*^9}, {3.9789933744434423`*^9, 
  3.978993379509547*^9}, {3.979344018131757*^9, 3.9793440233696623`*^9}, {
  3.979344100539311*^9, 3.979344100979267*^9}, {3.9800753134672213`*^9, 
  3.9800754005904818`*^9}, {3.980075451554854*^9, 
  3.980075455174108*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d877b8e0-68d9-4b63-b042-\
e07159824cb0"],

Cell["\<\
It seems that coordinates, reference frames, zero points, origins, and bases \
are all so deeply related, regarding purpose and necessity, that we can call \
all of them \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauges\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and we can \
call the activities of setting them up as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]setting \
gauge\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]choosing gauge.\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978884356699004*^9, 3.978884491775428*^9}, {
  3.9788845347619467`*^9, 3.978884683462042*^9}, {3.978884806945133*^9, 
  3.978885107805743*^9}, {3.9788851804396267`*^9, 3.978885192184779*^9}, {
  3.978885388709526*^9, 3.978885417081642*^9}, {3.97888545395669*^9, 
  3.9788854714725657`*^9}, {3.978890798743556*^9, 3.978890951740781*^9}, {
  3.978993439970787*^9, 3.978993449191094*^9}, {3.980075476224164*^9, 
  3.980075479650846*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4d3f9000-3f08-4efd-9c5b-\
4d797f7f05aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now, to the surprising statement: ",
 StyleBox["All Forces Arise from Choice of Gauge",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978885109029606*^9, 3.978885121222014*^9}, {
  3.97888515423064*^9, 3.978885172688307*^9}, {3.978885212632164*^9, 
  3.978885361306725*^9}, {3.97888550792782*^9, 3.978885642401931*^9}, {
  3.978885674820166*^9, 
  3.978885836835684*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3af05bdb-0e0c-4f7c-a3b7-\
590af72b3ae2"],

Cell["\<\
We\[CloseCurlyQuote]re not accustomed to this idea. We imagine forces as \
intrinsic physics, independent of gauges set to measure them. Planets are \
attracted to the Sun by a gravitational force, and we get compatible results \
in all reference frames. Electrons float around atomic nuclei by the same \
attractive Coulomb force, no matter how we measure it. Springs and pulleys \
apply forces to loads, no matter how we measure them.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978885109029606*^9, 3.978885121222014*^9}, {
  3.97888515423064*^9, 3.978885172688307*^9}, {3.978885212632164*^9, 
  3.978885361306725*^9}, {3.97888550792782*^9, 3.978885642401931*^9}, {
  3.978885674820166*^9, 3.978885812547159*^9}, {3.978885863653344*^9, 
  3.978886211180956*^9}, {3.978890974360463*^9, 3.9788912208949947`*^9}, {
  3.9788913800853167`*^9, 3.978891401200862*^9}, {3.978993496205426*^9, 
  3.978993565968006*^9}, {3.979344143227749*^9, 3.97934417930508*^9}, {
  3.98007607582568*^9, 
  3.980076082872994*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6dc2a9be-aed9-49ac-85e2-\
3a76f1e261dd"],

Cell["\<\
But forces change motions, and motions must be measured in coordinate \
systems, i.e., gauges. Different choices of gauge yield different values for \
motion measurements, so different gauges imply different forces to produce \
the observed motions. Some of these forces are only apparent, such as \
centrifugal and Coriolis forces. We can make these go away by choosing \
different a different gauge, say an inertial frame. Other forces are such \
that no choice of gauge can make them go away. The electric force is like \
that, and so is geodesic deviation, the ineluctable tidal force in curved \
spacetime. Choice of gauge will lead to different measurements, but \
invariances due to unavoidable symmetries in gauge choices reveal conserved \
quantities, which are the same in all gauges. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978885109029606*^9, 3.978885121222014*^9}, {
  3.97888515423064*^9, 3.978885172688307*^9}, {3.978885212632164*^9, 
  3.978885361306725*^9}, {3.97888550792782*^9, 3.978885642401931*^9}, {
  3.978885674820166*^9, 3.978885812547159*^9}, {3.978885863653344*^9, 
  3.978886211180956*^9}, {3.978890974360463*^9, 3.9788912208949947`*^9}, {
  3.9788913800853167`*^9, 3.978891393439958*^9}, {3.978891425714519*^9, 
  3.978891476565702*^9}, {3.978993579388056*^9, 3.978993610294231*^9}, {
  3.978993643391135*^9, 3.97899368930263*^9}, {3.9793442068352337`*^9, 
  3.9793442587695923`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"350d813e-d370-45ad-be4a-\
235e3b2f2073"],

Cell["\<\
Choice of gauge can change quantities other than force, like phase. By \
finding the symmetries\[LongDash]the choices of gauge that don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t change the physics\[LongDash]we find conservation laws \
via Noether\[CloseCurlyQuote]s theorem. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978885109029606*^9, 3.978885121222014*^9}, {
   3.97888515423064*^9, 3.978885172688307*^9}, {3.978885212632164*^9, 
   3.978885361306725*^9}, {3.97888550792782*^9, 3.978885642401931*^9}, {
   3.978885674820166*^9, 3.978885812547159*^9}, {3.978885863653344*^9, 
   3.978886211180956*^9}, {3.978890974360463*^9, 3.9788912208949947`*^9}, {
   3.9788913800853167`*^9, 3.978891393439958*^9}, {3.978891425714519*^9, 
   3.978891741930249*^9}, 3.9788921036239643`*^9, {3.978993696429472*^9, 
   3.978993703402165*^9}, 3.978993739923513*^9, {3.9793442737113323`*^9, 
   3.979344300713045*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0866725d-f7e1-463a-a22f-\
8cc36fc32856"],

Cell["\<\
When choice of the zero of stopwatches doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t affect the \
physics, i.e., when the physics is invariant with gauge choice for time, \
i.e., when time symmetry obtains, then energy is conserved. \
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978885109029606*^9, 3.978885121222014*^9}, {
   3.97888515423064*^9, 3.978885172688307*^9}, {3.978885212632164*^9, 
   3.978885361306725*^9}, {3.97888550792782*^9, 3.978885642401931*^9}, {
   3.978885674820166*^9, 3.978885812547159*^9}, {3.978885863653344*^9, 
   3.978886211180956*^9}, {3.978890974360463*^9, 3.9788912208949947`*^9}, {
   3.9788913800853167`*^9, 3.978891393439958*^9}, {3.978891425714519*^9, 
   3.978891741930249*^9}, 3.9788921036239643`*^9, {3.978993696429472*^9, 
   3.978993703402165*^9}, 3.978993743635854*^9, {3.9800761679050713`*^9, 
   3.9800761807684517`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8eddd732-3f83-44a3-a101-\
a3a684113622"],

Cell["\<\
When choice of the zero of position measurements doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
affect the physics, i.e., when the physics is invariant with gauge choice for \
position, i.e., when position symmetry obtains, momentum is conserved. \
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978885109029606*^9, 3.978885121222014*^9}, {
   3.97888515423064*^9, 3.978885172688307*^9}, {3.978885212632164*^9, 
   3.978885361306725*^9}, {3.97888550792782*^9, 3.978885642401931*^9}, {
   3.978885674820166*^9, 3.978885812547159*^9}, {3.978885863653344*^9, 
   3.978886211180956*^9}, {3.978890974360463*^9, 3.9788912208949947`*^9}, {
   3.9788913800853167`*^9, 3.978891393439958*^9}, {3.978891425714519*^9, 
   3.978891741930249*^9}, 3.9788921036239643`*^9, {3.978993696429472*^9, 
   3.978993703402165*^9}, 3.97899374809756*^9, {3.980076187241222*^9, 
   3.98007619164601*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c0a09dd3-28b0-439a-8a14-\
49b734938b7d"],

Cell["\<\
When choice of a zero for phase doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t affect the physics, \
i.e., when the physics is invariant with gauge choice for phase, i.e., when \
phase symmetry obtains, electric charge is conserved.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978885109029606*^9, 3.978885121222014*^9}, {
   3.97888515423064*^9, 3.978885172688307*^9}, {3.978885212632164*^9, 
   3.978885361306725*^9}, {3.97888550792782*^9, 3.978885642401931*^9}, {
   3.978885674820166*^9, 3.978885812547159*^9}, {3.978885863653344*^9, 
   3.978886211180956*^9}, {3.978890974360463*^9, 3.9788912208949947`*^9}, {
   3.9788913800853167`*^9, 3.978891393439958*^9}, {3.978891425714519*^9, 
   3.978891741930249*^9}, 3.9788921036239643`*^9, {3.978993696429472*^9, 
   3.978993703402165*^9}, 3.978993753657466*^9, {3.980076197959374*^9, 
   3.980076204221287*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"aaf89443-6ba5-4f26-9897-\
75d3de0e13a1"],

Cell["\<\
 And so on. E.g., invariance to unitary transformations in nuclear physics: \
hypercharge and color charge are conserved. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978885109029606*^9, 3.978885121222014*^9}, {
   3.97888515423064*^9, 3.978885172688307*^9}, {3.978885212632164*^9, 
   3.978885361306725*^9}, {3.97888550792782*^9, 3.978885642401931*^9}, {
   3.978885674820166*^9, 3.978885812547159*^9}, {3.978885863653344*^9, 
   3.978886211180956*^9}, {3.978890974360463*^9, 3.9788912208949947`*^9}, {
   3.9788913800853167`*^9, 3.978891393439958*^9}, {3.978891425714519*^9, 
   3.978891741930249*^9}, 3.9788921036239643`*^9, {3.978993696429472*^9, 
   3.978993703402165*^9}, {3.978993762625421*^9, 3.978993767018323*^9}, {
   3.9800762191196423`*^9, 
   3.980076224932418*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e80ef5d6-3b9d-4c98-aa23-\
35b5f98e38eb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["We Hear Too Late about Gauge", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978993805850855*^9, 
  3.978993848588606*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9de053a9-2f3a-4072-9ca2-\
05fa574c4950"],

Cell["\<\
In elementary physics, we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t call choice of reference \
frame a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge choice.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Nor do \
we hear the exotic idea that gauge choice generates force. But such is the \
case. For an elementary example, consider measuring the altitude of an Earth \
satellite flying in a stable, circular, free-fall orbit. If we measure \
altitude with respect to mean sea level, the satellite seems to have a \
constant altitude, Earth\[CloseCurlyQuote]s oblateness aside, and we measure \
no forces on it. However, if we measure altitude with respect to the \
irregular surface of the Earth, the satellite\[CloseCurlyQuote]s altitude \
varies madly up and down. To naive observers, unaware of this poor choice of \
gauge, the satellite appears to suffer inexplicable forces pushing it up and \
down. However, these apparent forces arise merely from the choice of gauge. \
Here, the term \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] fits \
entirely with its ordinary, dictionary meaning, as an altimeter with its \
arbitrary, and possibly locally variable, origin setting. An even more \
elementary example is a rotating reference frame. Measure positions and \
momenta of free particles in an inertial lab frame, see no forces. If, \
however, we measure from a rotating frame, we see centrifugal and Coriolis \
forces, arising merely from the choice of gauge, of reference frame.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786386648875933`*^9, 3.978639147971436*^9}, {
   3.9786401089109507`*^9, 3.97864013021977*^9}, {3.978640191966693*^9, 
   3.978640516557682*^9}, {3.978641281651569*^9, 3.9786412836572237`*^9}, {
   3.978737855552356*^9, 3.9787379905163193`*^9}, {3.9787380221754427`*^9, 
   3.978738036037778*^9}, {3.9787889122095747`*^9, 3.978789038628954*^9}, {
   3.978789131640423*^9, 3.978789330099185*^9}, {3.978789377753706*^9, 
   3.978789388367732*^9}, {3.978789489346162*^9, 3.9787895396860113`*^9}, {
   3.9787897001908827`*^9, 3.978789714267542*^9}, 3.978885857551659*^9, {
   3.978886224258911*^9, 3.978886428261237*^9}, {3.9788906071764517`*^9, 
   3.978890635004664*^9}, {3.978891762886993*^9, 3.978891905668881*^9}, {
   3.9789938747222223`*^9, 3.978993881854785*^9}, {3.978993914931596*^9, 
   3.978993923295239*^9}, {3.979344442760394*^9, 3.9793444701827297`*^9}, {
   3.980076298794189*^9, 
   3.980076329535811*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3b439049-7cf4-4a34-bc54-\
20d77b2ca349"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Gauge theory is totally pertinent to classical mechanics, but physics \
students don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t study \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] until classical electrodynamics, where gauge an \
abstract, unobservable, ",
 StyleBox["arbitrary",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox[" field",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " whose ",
 StyleBox["gradient",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is added to the vector potential. How much farther from reality can you \
get? There is no conceivable relationship of this idea to the dictionary \
meaning of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] By the time \
our students get to electrodynamics, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s too late to go \
back and review the forces of elementary mechanics as arising from gauge \
choice. Our unfortunate students will carry multiple bags, all the way \
through general relativity (GR), with \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] a demonic, ephemeral concept at best, until it \
appears again as even more abstract fields of complex matrices in particle \
physics. Our students could have packed all these ideas into one piece of \
baggage with a concrete view of gauge as just a choice of reference frame, \
varying from the concrete to the abstract, from the scalar to tensor, from \
the Reals to the Complex, but just a reference frame nonetheless."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978639302944932*^9, 3.978639559880187*^9}, {
   3.978639906097765*^9, 3.97863990678701*^9}, 3.978639968293231*^9, {
   3.9786400579528627`*^9, 3.9786400802416973`*^9}, {3.978640595978593*^9, 
   3.9786408470755568`*^9}, {3.978641348822749*^9, 3.97864137181462*^9}, {
   3.978738070996792*^9, 3.9787380861994247`*^9}, {3.978789438625586*^9, 
   3.978789478159536*^9}, {3.9787895499480867`*^9, 3.97878968026201*^9}, {
   3.978789744864238*^9, 3.978789876297686*^9}, {3.9787914565016108`*^9, 
   3.978791457765832*^9}, {3.9788864631668787`*^9, 3.978886628738146*^9}, {
   3.9788919247952213`*^9, 3.978892027927437*^9}, {3.9789939701608477`*^9, 
   3.9789940801535063`*^9}, {3.979344545726364*^9, 3.979344610518824*^9}, {
   3.979344643069969*^9, 3.979344740905566*^9}, {3.9800763879499903`*^9, 
   3.980076487377336*^9}, {3.980076527117703*^9, 
   3.9800765283802147`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6ceec6ac-1964-4e3a-8308-\
bc09bb1272c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And then, knowing that ",
 StyleBox["all forces, apparent or fundamental, do, in fact, arise from \
choice of gauge",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", and knowing that gauge symmetries drive conservation laws, we can put the \
travel sticker \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Noether\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] on our \
one remaining piece of baggage and get \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Noether\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] visa stamps in our passports as we journey through \
all of physics. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978640894250175*^9, 3.978641074879751*^9}, {
  3.978641407380624*^9, 3.9786414732143106`*^9}, {3.9786420394434547`*^9, 
  3.978642039792768*^9}, {3.9787381300235453`*^9, 3.978738138526342*^9}, {
  3.978789896455791*^9, 3.978789928750749*^9}, {3.97889206846725*^9, 
  3.978892073109419*^9}, {3.97889211544514*^9, 3.978892136225336*^9}, {
  3.9789940978389053`*^9, 3.978994214869359*^9}, {3.979344757454185*^9, 
  3.979344826700527*^9}, {3.9800765482135057`*^9, 
  3.980076594564807*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"38b64028-6be8-42fb-8046-\
17cfbe0c10fc"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gauge Forces as Connections", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786365673927803`*^9, 3.9786365728569317`*^9}, {
  3.978637906305097*^9, 3.978637911784799*^9}, {3.978641629594967*^9, 
  3.978641632842622*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"de2e5ba2-e25c-4f93-bcd4-\
a727b1f176d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How, exactly, do forces arise from gauge? Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s see how \
gauge ",
 StyleBox["connections",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", our old friends from the covariant derivative, are the ultimate source of \
force. Recall from earlier notebooks that in GR, the Christoffel symbols are \
the connections that separate intrinsic curvature of spacetime, which no \
choice of gauge can eliminate, from extrinsic curvature caused by choice of \
coordinates. At a single point, we can always choose a local inertial frame, \
a gauge, that makes Christoffel symbols vanish, and acceleration, thus force, \
go away. This is Einstein\[CloseCurlyQuote]s famous \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]elevator\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] demonstration of the \
Principle of Equivalence. But the paths of two particles, initially parallel, \
will converge or diverge in a curved spacetime, and no choice of gauge can \
make the resulting \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]tidal \
forces\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] go away. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978892159885597*^9, 3.9788925530731297`*^9}, {
  3.9789942436513853`*^9, 3.978994280384554*^9}, {3.97934485691464*^9, 
  3.9793448931127234`*^9}, {3.979344933058769*^9, 3.979344936447179*^9}, {
  3.980076610493311*^9, 
  3.980076708096345*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"47cc3ea8-c3ee-493d-ab91-\
486ca4e36c3e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve studied covariant derivative, connections, and \
Christoffel symbols in this series of notebooks, specifically in GR. We\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve repeatedly read that we can and should recast these \
ideas in terms of gauge theory, but we\[CloseCurlyQuote]re not told how to do \
that. Now is the time, with the clarity that gauge choice is just choice of \
reference frame, though in a generalized sense. ",
 StyleBox["Geometrical",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " frame invariance, now geometrical gauge invariance, the choice of time and \
space coordinates for measurements, drives the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]discovery\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of covariant \
derivative and connection. Connection drives equations of motion, thus \
forces, for Schwarzschild orbits. We\[CloseCurlyQuote]re now equipped to \
study the other forces of Nature on the same terms."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978641572817196*^9, 3.978641680574541*^9}, {
  3.9786417137944403`*^9, 3.9786418997181177`*^9}, {3.978641933868432*^9, 
  3.978641951159326*^9}, {3.978738177896667*^9, 3.9787382112497663`*^9}, {
  3.978789968088002*^9, 3.9787900903971*^9}, {3.978892571678391*^9, 
  3.978892607783853*^9}, {3.978892650696258*^9, 3.978892745998905*^9}, {
  3.978994324299697*^9, 3.978994364496356*^9}, {3.980076731860106*^9, 
  3.9800768448152933`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1a069641-6cc6-4768-99db-\
9d7dbb563bb2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Back to our physics students. This time, in life v2.0, with lighter, \
Noether-tagged baggage, they encounter gauge again, ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for the first time, in classical electrodynamics. They realize that the \
gradient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"da405388-5867-4920-baa6-f97f29301ff3"],
 " of any differentiable scalar field \[CapitalLambda], rightfully called a \
gauge field, can be added to the vector potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["A", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "045e9d27-5d95-4ecc-9cd4-52d87947a806"],
 " without altering the physics:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978636576303603*^9, 3.9786366785799294`*^9}, {
   3.978636723696795*^9, 3.978636870996152*^9}, {3.978636910194687*^9, 
   3.978636921670682*^9}, {3.9786370048263483`*^9, 3.9786370849609137`*^9}, 
   3.978637277938579*^9, {3.9786380563234453`*^9, 3.978638089888694*^9}, {
   3.978641485319695*^9, 3.9786415366166553`*^9}, {3.9786419540622797`*^9, 
   3.9786419851870832`*^9}, {3.978738229613509*^9, 3.978738232163897*^9}, {
   3.978738275893861*^9, 3.9787382803704367`*^9}, {3.978790103133443*^9, 
   3.978790176728155*^9}, {3.978892765869252*^9, 3.978892767609643*^9}, {
   3.978994371249153*^9, 3.9789943814530067`*^9}, {3.979344998492833*^9, 
   3.9793450598032227`*^9}, {3.979345121341195*^9, 3.979345127324295*^9}, {
   3.979345796506509*^9, 3.9793458111374817`*^9}, {3.9800768779950542`*^9, 
   3.980076905836988*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a613ee36-0c11-41f8-a3ac-\
7ed05a5d6d67"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["A", "_"], 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "(", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "(", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637090481073*^9, 3.978637121098152*^9}, {
  3.9786372899247313`*^9, 3.978637455330873*^9}, {3.978637578634162*^9, 
  3.978637584593306*^9}, {3.978638122624658*^9, 3.978638130156509*^9}, {
  3.9788934388431053`*^9, 
  3.978893442850831*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"32584ea5-15fb-48bb-b029-\
3d8673cac545"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ok, \[CapitalLambda] is a gauge field, but in what sense is \
\[CapitalLambda] the choice of a reference frame, in fact, as the choice of \
an uncountable infinity of reference frames, one at each point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Nu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "235fca82-31f7-4cec-99b1-15a081c8dece"],
 "? "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978636576303603*^9, 3.9786366785799294`*^9}, {
  3.978636723696795*^9, 3.978636870996152*^9}, {3.978636910194687*^9, 
  3.978636921670682*^9}, {3.9786370048263483`*^9, 3.978637074091062*^9}, {
  3.9786374735329943`*^9, 3.97863749900111*^9}, {3.9786420889624434`*^9, 
  3.978642183847044*^9}, {3.978645450479156*^9, 3.978645504372199*^9}, {
  3.978738291981337*^9, 3.978738457947143*^9}, {3.978790183027944*^9, 
  3.9787902062151537`*^9}, {3.978790241679438*^9, 3.978790364497869*^9}, {
  3.978892790924198*^9, 3.978892912225272*^9}, {3.978994406922344*^9, 
  3.9789944077971983`*^9}, {3.979345137399835*^9, 3.979345182434143*^9}, {
  3.980076936830947*^9, 
  3.9800770138417463`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f0ddc887-eb41-41eb-9130-\
415710d079c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Well, electrodynamical gauge invariance is ",
 StyleBox["also ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "presented as ",
 StyleBox["phase invariance",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", a factor of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
    RowBox[{" ", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"57fda5bf-ae22-46b2-a1f8-10c25493e4fd"],
 " (same \[CapitalLambda]) that can be multiplied into a charged matter field \
\[Psi] without altering the physics. Spoiler: choose phase with respect to an \
arbitrary zero. This is the ",
 StyleBox["primary",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " principle of electrodynamical gauge as a coordinate frame. Gradient added \
to vector potential (Equation 1) is just the ",
 StyleBox["mechanism",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]induced \
transformation,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] that upholds that principle. Here\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s how that works:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978636576303603*^9, 3.9786366785799294`*^9}, {
  3.978636723696795*^9, 3.978636870996152*^9}, {3.978636910194687*^9, 
  3.978636921670682*^9}, {3.9786370048263483`*^9, 3.978637074091062*^9}, {
  3.9786374735329943`*^9, 3.97863749900111*^9}, {3.9786420889624434`*^9, 
  3.978642183847044*^9}, {3.978645450479156*^9, 3.978645504372199*^9}, {
  3.978738291981337*^9, 3.978738457947143*^9}, {3.978790183027944*^9, 
  3.9787902062151537`*^9}, {3.978790241679438*^9, 3.978790364497869*^9}, {
  3.978892790924198*^9, 3.978892912225272*^9}, {3.978994406922344*^9, 
  3.9789944077971983`*^9}, {3.979345137399835*^9, 3.979345182434143*^9}, {
  3.980076936830947*^9, 
  3.980077092732531*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"64ce8178-c352-4270-b915-\
4e9e76600bbf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Change a matter field \[Psi] by rotating its phase (gauge) by an arbitrary \
(but smoothly varying) amount, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8887eb8f-8e50-4c43-bc2b-5fa6ed172500"],
 ", at every point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "148377dc-a2d4-4c2d-ad37-7d9e8c50c6fa"],
 ", without changing the geometrical coordinates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "495da672-5450-4bd6-abfa-24210b59bf10"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637538672182*^9, 3.978637755565897*^9}, {
  3.978642236477104*^9, 3.978642246171332*^9}, {3.9787903747991543`*^9, 
  3.978790376943686*^9}, {3.978821792309321*^9, 3.978821810066669*^9}, {
  3.978892930168849*^9, 
  3.9788929308418903`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bbd91da1-9c66-4a41-b4ca-\
51cbc1f36766"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], "(", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
        SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}]], "\[Psi]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637538672182*^9, 3.97863778411996*^9}, {
  3.9786379712287197`*^9, 3.9786379796646557`*^9}, {3.978821290744693*^9, 
  3.978821330476513*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2699533f-e0e2-4931-b108-\
e52ba5a0a837"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is just like choosing a reference-frame origin for the phase of the \
matter fields, locally, at each point, without changing the spacetime \
geometry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Nu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ca3bbc6-264a-495c-8f82-6aea542239d5"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978642193583212*^9, 3.978642224078884*^9}, {
  3.9787384986624413`*^9, 3.978738566270625*^9}, {3.978790924023786*^9, 
  3.978790949934161*^9}, {3.978821303008254*^9, 3.9788213409196463`*^9}, {
  3.9788218407423058`*^9, 3.978821903531654*^9}, {3.9788929458880177`*^9, 
  3.978892966706778*^9}, {3.9793458429854393`*^9, 3.9793458528593893`*^9}, {
  3.980077504995469*^9, 
  3.980077538574395*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2f9bbb0b-d116-44fa-86dd-\
f610d75178b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take the ordinary partial derivative, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dbe210c8-941f-4a8e-b180-8f7245a144d6"],
 ", of this new field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cb83cb2a-980f-4291-9ce1-09b15724f99f"],
 ". The ordinary product rule of differentiation spits out a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]garbage term\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CapitalLambda]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "140f5d75-b68e-465c-9c4e-2609eda551b2"],
 " varies with position:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637795314996*^9, 3.9786378832705383`*^9}, {
  3.978638180667034*^9, 3.9786381881906633`*^9}, {3.978642259537039*^9, 
  3.978642260939106*^9}, {3.978738583002688*^9, 3.978738586607667*^9}, {
  3.978790411450951*^9, 3.9787904159652767`*^9}, {3.9789944754159803`*^9, 
  3.978994478279684*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d709d7b9-a0b8-444c-a891-\
799112cdd05f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], "(", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
         SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}]], "  ", 
     RowBox[{"(", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
        RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "(", 
         SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"i", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "(", 
         SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Nu]"], ")"}]}]}], "  ", ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
   "or", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "abbreviating", " ", "away", " ", "the", " ", "spacetime", " ", 
    "coordinates"}]}], TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "  ", 
    RowBox[{"(", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"i", "(", 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
       "\[Psi]"}]}], "  ", ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]}], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637887868793*^9, 3.9786378947514553`*^9}, {
  3.978637927473442*^9, 3.9786379497151003`*^9}, {3.978637985585307*^9, 
  3.9786380459954576`*^9}, {3.978638197487301*^9, 3.97863825659056*^9}, {
  3.978790463257308*^9, 3.978790502671747*^9}, {3.978790553765525*^9, 
  3.978790557365933*^9}, {3.978994489314309*^9, 
  3.978994495696596*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"62e7a310-9def-4de0-b41b-\
525e0f7c85ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sound familiar? This is exactly what happened in relativity. The \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]garbage terms\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (Hessians) drove \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]discovery\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of covariant \
derivative and connection coefficients. Here, likewise, the extra term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"i", "(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
    "\[Psi]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637887868793*^9, 3.9786378947514553`*^9}, {
   3.978637927473442*^9, 3.9786379497151003`*^9}, {3.978637985585307*^9, 
   3.9786380459954576`*^9}, {3.978638197487301*^9, 3.97863825659056*^9}},
  ExpressionUUID->"2d5d94d4-52a6-4301-98a1-27bff23628c1"],
 " ruins the physics. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978638433441883*^9, 3.978638454013837*^9}, {
   3.978638510142865*^9, 3.978638525977479*^9}, {3.978638574219385*^9, 
   3.9786385939606123`*^9}, {3.9786423189988194`*^9, 3.978642326146699*^9}, {
   3.978790523634274*^9, 3.97879052765222*^9}, {3.978790577036037*^9, 
   3.978790824183269*^9}, {3.978790987080504*^9, 3.978790987746471*^9}, {
   3.9788219390917053`*^9, 3.9788219693335457`*^9}, 3.978892993643753*^9, {
   3.978994510384351*^9, 3.978994524094184*^9}, {3.980077560622377*^9, 
   3.9800775727466908`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b44631bb-d396-4767-9ec4-\
dc3c65c2de71"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As before, we find that the ordinary derivative is not covariant: it doesn\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t survive changes in phase coordinates, arbitrary changes \
in choice of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"082faf35-4189-409e-8dc6-848f267cad22"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978638433441883*^9, 3.978638454013837*^9}, {
  3.978638510142865*^9, 3.978638525977479*^9}, {3.978638574219385*^9, 
  3.9786385939606123`*^9}, {3.9786423189988194`*^9, 3.978642326146699*^9}, {
  3.978790523634274*^9, 3.97879052765222*^9}, {3.978790577036037*^9, 
  3.978790824183269*^9}, {3.978790987080504*^9, 3.978790987746471*^9}, {
  3.9788219390917053`*^9, 3.9788219693335457`*^9}, {3.978893006505972*^9, 
  3.9788930214632883`*^9}, {3.978994536826796*^9, 
  3.97899453984762*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dbf40625-fe82-4da4-a1a5-\
751f51c303cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In GR, the gauge was spacetime geometry itself, so compensating for \
coordinate change required 4D index manipulation. With electrodynamics, \
compensating for phase changes is easier. The ",
 StyleBox["electrodynamical connection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a one-index object because the electrodynamical gauge field \
\[CapitalLambda] is one-dimensional."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643141459524*^9, 3.9786431828556843`*^9}, {
  3.978738641173134*^9, 3.9787386532797832`*^9}, {3.9787908465552607`*^9, 
  3.978790856317902*^9}, {3.978791011986392*^9, 3.9787911783544617`*^9}, {
  3.978821976523123*^9, 3.978821990362543*^9}, {3.978893035332219*^9, 
  3.9788930933004837`*^9}, {3.978893176148498*^9, 3.97889319198171*^9}, {
  3.978893340101403*^9, 3.978893376381797*^9}, {3.9789945517648907`*^9, 
  3.978994565683864*^9}, {3.980077598925391*^9, 
  3.980077599085737*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3414dda7-eeae-4408-b9c8-\
65d7bb7ac439"],

Cell["\<\
To clean up the electrodynamical gauge garbage, we need a correction term in \
our covariant derivative of the matter field, just as we did with geometry \
and GR:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643216420027*^9, 3.978643271965823*^9}, {
  3.978791185639865*^9, 3.978791190604082*^9}, {3.978893115500826*^9, 
  3.978893118477109*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c3bdd501-64cd-4593-9110-\
51b97f3a3483"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Congruent]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
     RowBox[{"-", "i"}]}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643276164227*^9, 3.9786432889746*^9}, {
  3.978643322108322*^9, 3.978643337180196*^9}, {3.978643475279353*^9, 
  3.978643475281219*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4b3596e5-775e-4090-a055-\
8eaa17ef6d01"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Yes, the connection is the vector potential, hence it drives \
electrodynamical forces",
 StyleBox[", just as the Christoffel (Levi-Civita) connection drives \
gravitational forces. Equation 1 specifies how the connection changes with \
change of gauge. Notice this connection does not transform like \[Psi] with \
change of \[CapitalLambda], just as the Christoffel symbols don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t transform like tensors with change of spacetime \
coordinates. Connections aren\[CloseCurlyQuote]t tensorial.",
  FontWeight->"Plain"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786433489592524`*^9, 3.978643399831469*^9}, {
  3.978643451260046*^9, 3.9786434570432673`*^9}, {3.978738674339534*^9, 
  3.9787386751608458`*^9}, {3.978791202722198*^9, 3.978791212226269*^9}, {
  3.97899458832428*^9, 3.978994619099072*^9}, {3.979348206495863*^9, 
  3.9793482538617764`*^9}, {3.979348294441743*^9, 3.9793483430094147`*^9}, {
  3.9800776761984386`*^9, 3.980077683674735*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"4bf37e51-2ef4-47e2-827e-789c2120b0a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]re going to change the geometrical, spacetime \
coordinate system. For the garbage terms to cancel out exactly, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2067fddd-8cc5-4abc-aa7a-b8e8d364c7cf"],
 " must transform as in Equation 1 (abbreviated):"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980077743784195*^9, 
  3.9800777899879217`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"057e8e04-9c4e-44c8-81a3-\
c8b7aead3567"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox["A", "_"], 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["A", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637090481073*^9, 3.978637121098152*^9}, {
  3.9786372899247313`*^9, 3.978637455330873*^9}, {3.978637578634162*^9, 
  3.978637584593306*^9}, {3.978638122624658*^9, 3.978638130156509*^9}, {
  3.9786434831358967`*^9, 
  3.978643484399239*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8246d647-b649-43c2-88f5-\
751f17de6404"],

Cell["We have the new covariant derivative", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643488286076*^9, 3.9786434909815903`*^9}, {
   3.978791254151824*^9, 3.978791255677359*^9}, 3.978893471681477*^9, {
   3.978994645083848*^9, 
   3.978994650356408*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"da41081c-7849-4055-973c-\
2f4774d27dcb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "\[Congruent]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786435032056303`*^9, 
  3.978643606837364*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"024e8a50-8217-4ff4-b17b-\
0b0e6867c4b7"],

Cell["and", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978643593775935*^9, 
  3.978643594327322*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"32719714-8e0a-4b65-8a22-\
07f3d69ea5fc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], 
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
      OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox["A", "_"], "\[Mu]"], 
      OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"i", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
         "\[Psi]"}]}], ")"}]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox["A", "_"], "\[Mu]"], 
      OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"i", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
        "\[Psi]"}]}], ")"}]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"i", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["A", 
        RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
        RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
         RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "\[Psi]"}],
       ")"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}], 
    StyleBox["+",
     FontVariations->{"StrikeThrough"->True}], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "i", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
      "\[Psi]"}],
     FontVariations->{"StrikeThrough"->True}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "\[Psi]"}], 
    StyleBox["-",
     FontVariations->{"StrikeThrough"->True}], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "i", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]"}], ")"}], 
      "\[Psi]"}],
     FontVariations->{"StrikeThrough"->True}]}]}], TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "\[Psi]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm], "\[LineSeparator]", 
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "(", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      SubscriptBox["A", 
       RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "\[Psi]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]}], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786436192725773`*^9, 3.9786437727905197`*^9}, {
  3.978643806573044*^9, 3.978643946308076*^9}, {3.978644002327197*^9, 
  3.978644220022155*^9}, {3.978644291740561*^9, 3.9786443538434763`*^9}, {
  3.978644388511799*^9, 
  3.978644510127365*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a5eab264-474f-4226-a0ae-\
4d3f337c5c42"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
  CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786435032056303`*^9, 3.978643606837364*^9}},
  ExpressionUUID->"7733d1c6-ae39-495d-a43c-c2abb504c5c3"],
 " transforms \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]covariantly\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in \
gauge space by multiplying by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"f62119a8-fc0b-4fd7-9e74-1ff13ac97789"],
 ", even though ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6a6c1a57-db68-4e98-a191-0584e3e8b892"],
 " does not transform covariantly in this way. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97864452629532*^9, 3.9786446238462*^9}, 
   3.978738689142243*^9, {3.978738724694315*^9, 3.978738784872237*^9}, {
   3.978791265368784*^9, 3.9787913061211567`*^9}, {3.978893496419726*^9, 
   3.978893632712524*^9}, {3.9793483901312838`*^9, 3.97934843153382*^9}, {
   3.979348530626459*^9, 3.9793487401127043`*^9}, {3.9800778267980967`*^9, 
   3.980077827602209*^9}, {3.980077867009365*^9, 3.980077983849736*^9}, {
   3.9800875089195957`*^9, 3.9800875134607763`*^9}, {3.980087728594531*^9, 
   3.9800877508155317`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6e85698d-954f-469b-848a-\
601c91c29c9b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It so happens that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6cbeb492-8b07-4793-9fa0-90b7289e1359"],
 " is, geometrically, a covariant covector, so it ",
 StyleBox["does ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "transforms covariantly with change in coordinates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Nu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2cb72396-7c4d-412b-9e69-2f4c2eee5760"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97864452629532*^9, 3.9786446238462*^9}, 
   3.978738689142243*^9, {3.978738724694315*^9, 3.978738784872237*^9}, {
   3.978791265368784*^9, 3.9787913061211567`*^9}, {3.978893496419726*^9, 
   3.978893632712524*^9}, {3.9793483901312838`*^9, 3.97934843153382*^9}, {
   3.979348530626459*^9, 3.9793487401127043`*^9}, {3.9800778267980967`*^9, 
   3.980077827602209*^9}, {3.980077867009365*^9, 3.980077983849736*^9}, {
   3.9800875089195957`*^9, 3.9800875134607763`*^9}, {3.980087728594531*^9, 
   3.980087743675682*^9}, {3.980087776726445*^9, 
   3.9800878238947973`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c22bb146-47b3-4f7d-820b-\
812116ce0817"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The geometrical covariant derivative from GR transforms covariantly with \
geometrical coordinates. The gauge covariant derivative, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["D", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc59e78-9d32-4c67-bc7c-66057340842a"],
 ", transforms covariantly with phase, i.e., gauge coordinates. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97864452629532*^9, 3.9786446238462*^9}, 
   3.978738689142243*^9, {3.978738724694315*^9, 3.978738784872237*^9}, {
   3.978791265368784*^9, 3.9787913061211567`*^9}, {3.978893496419726*^9, 
   3.978893632712524*^9}, {3.9793483901312838`*^9, 3.97934843153382*^9}, {
   3.979348530626459*^9, 3.9793487401127043`*^9}, {3.9800778267980967`*^9, 
   3.980077827602209*^9}, {3.980077867009365*^9, 3.980077983849736*^9}, {
   3.9800875089195957`*^9, 3.9800875134607763`*^9}, {3.980087728594531*^9, 
   3.980087743675682*^9}, {3.980087776726445*^9, 
   3.9800878306514893`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"18a9dcce-fa20-4f0f-9165-\
b7030bfc77e7"],

Cell["\<\
Two covariant derivatives, one against geometrical coordinates, the other \
against phase. One idea of covariance.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97864452629532*^9, 3.9786446238462*^9}, 
   3.978738689142243*^9, {3.978738724694315*^9, 3.978738784872237*^9}, {
   3.978791265368784*^9, 3.9787913061211567`*^9}, {3.978893496419726*^9, 
   3.978893632712524*^9}, {3.9793483901312838`*^9, 3.97934843153382*^9}, {
   3.979348530626459*^9, 3.9793487401127043`*^9}, {3.9800778267980967`*^9, 
   3.980077827602209*^9}, {3.980077867009365*^9, 3.980077983849736*^9}, {
   3.9800875089195957`*^9, 3.9800875134607763`*^9}, {3.980087728594531*^9, 
   3.980087743675682*^9}, {3.980087776726445*^9, 
   3.98008783979843*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"67c0190c-ffd0-418f-ad77-\
42ae7844de37"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["We now see why it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a good idea, after all, to \
call the covariant derivative ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "covariant",
 StyleBox[". Such honors the metaphor between \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]spacetime coordinates as spacetime gauge with its own \
covariant derivative\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]phase \
as gauge everywhere with its own covariant \
derivative,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] despite the fact that in geometry and GR, \
the covariant derivative also pertains to ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "contravariant",
 StyleBox[" indices, a fact we dismissed as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]historical\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in an earlier notebook.",
  FontSlant->"Italic"]
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978644642417985*^9, 3.978644753146748*^9}, {
  3.978645552948409*^9, 3.978645554732916*^9}, {3.978738701834901*^9, 
  3.978738704297278*^9}, {3.978893645016326*^9, 3.978893678782941*^9}, {
  3.979346847915805*^9, 3.979346904275305*^9}, {3.980087866214898*^9, 
  3.980087938722365*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3eaa4828-6fd0-4989-bab6-\
6e2697261d66"],

Cell["\<\
We\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll write some new functions for the Relativity Toolkit to \
automate the calculation above, after just one last setup section.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97864452629532*^9, 3.978644608759818*^9}, {
  3.9786447582836847`*^9, 3.978644803628751*^9}, {3.9786458816287622`*^9, 
  3.978645931893115*^9}, {3.978646349194942*^9, 3.978646350719452*^9}, {
  3.978791323640992*^9, 3.9787913558959093`*^9}, {3.978791495646101*^9, 
  3.9787915191520576`*^9}, {3.9800882324151907`*^9, 
  3.98008824772473*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ac12e704-4f80-48a5-b9da-\
4e11ea15a54f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Covariant Derivatives, Revisited", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978358251530368*^9, 
  3.978358274502495*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7f6b77f4-b0fc-4a67-b903-\
969955fdadc1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In GR, we learned to take covariant derivatives of tensors that inhabit the \
tangent and cotangent tensor spaces at each point of a curved manifold. The \
canonical example is the covariant derivative of an arbitrary contravariant \
vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["A", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a18ef1ef-909d-46ca-af3d-a413ac2c6455"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "6eafb1ad-e0f7-4fac-bd37-46969ee45354"],
 " not for not vector potential here! ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "41538242-b3a0-40a2-864e-511e3201e227"],
 " for arbitrary!) with respect geometrical coordinates:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.978645997660583*^9}, {
  3.9787915036557417`*^9, 3.978791531715695*^9}, {3.979348896909027*^9, 
  3.979348928838019*^9}, {3.980087977109717*^9, 3.9800880480484953`*^9}, {
  3.980088078321742*^9, 
  3.980088104515327*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4f010f30-76ff-4c9d-9e45-\
977a9562d116"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"example", "=", 
      RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
       RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"A", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Nu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
       "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Echo", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"TensorForm", "@@", "example"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"example", "\"\<\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978358547373548*^9, 3.978358772499927*^9}, {
  3.978359072474093*^9, 3.978359157811211*^9}, {3.9783592724273376`*^9, 
  3.978359272556822*^9}, {3.9783593063094587`*^9, 3.9783593921632147`*^9}, {
  3.978383680431888*^9, 3.978383735895418*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"78497388-807e-47b1-a2f3-54ab4ce22561"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{"\<\"\"\>", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     TagBox[
      SubscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"A", 
        SuperscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], 
       RowBox[{";", "\[Nu]"}]],
      HoldForm], ")"}]}],
   "EchoLabel"], "  ", 
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SuperscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], 
     RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"A", 
       SuperscriptBox["", "\[Lambda]"]}], ")"}], " ", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "\[Lambda]"}], "\[Mu]"]}]}],
   HoldForm]}]], "Echo",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.980088017103438*^9},ExpressionUUID->"63bbfcca-ac53-40ec-868d-\
526343b4ffa7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The connection coefficients \[CapitalGamma] account for twisting and \
turning of basis vectors in the tangent spaces as the vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["A", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dd3e6e84-9f68-483f-906e-506409ee1c30"],
 " is parallel-transported geometrically. In GR, this twisting and turning \
causes geodesics to converge or diverge, thus causing tidal forces. Twisting \
and turning also drives single geodesics, giving rise to orbits, \
gravitational lensing, gravitational waves, and so on."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.978646017572369*^9}, {
  3.978646073037752*^9, 3.978646096573864*^9}, {3.978791550457979*^9, 
  3.9787915716892157`*^9}, {3.978791607811911*^9, 3.978791645252721*^9}, {
  3.9789947228843813`*^9, 3.9789947833892727`*^9}, {3.979346935639179*^9, 
  3.9793469359737883`*^9}, {3.979348792711174*^9, 3.979348826305972*^9}, {
  3.980088125045064*^9, 
  3.98008817900523*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"37424616-b889-4f35-aa46-\
5f5a9d34df7f"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Emphasis: Geodesic deviation is indistinguishable \
from tidal force. It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s not an apparent force: its numerical \
values may depend on gauge choice, but we can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t get rid of \
it globally by gauge choice.",
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.978646017572369*^9}, {
  3.978646073037752*^9, 3.978646096573864*^9}, {3.978791550457979*^9, 
  3.9787915716892157`*^9}, {3.978791607811911*^9, 3.9787916688688183`*^9}, {
  3.978893726055107*^9, 3.978893734728683*^9}, {3.978994793962654*^9, 
  3.978994807936285*^9}, {3.979348947568865*^9, 3.979348965248041*^9}, {
  3.980088203867462*^9, 
  3.980088206557819*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a0d3e19d-b357-44b9-be80-\
c725fc844522"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The derivative above transforms like a tensor, ensuring physics is ",
 StyleBox["locally Lorentz invariant",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". This invariance invites Noether\[CloseCurlyQuote]s theorem again, \
implying a conserved quantity. In GR, this conserved quantity is ",
 StyleBox["spin current",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", from symmetries of non-coordinate bases or ",
 StyleBox["tetrads",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (see Appendix 1)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.97864602352232*^9}, {
  3.97864610862702*^9, 3.9786461676375427`*^9}, {3.978738857168982*^9, 
  3.978738864834247*^9}, {3.9787916844234667`*^9, 3.978791699695005*^9}, {
  3.978893751507414*^9, 3.978893784918326*^9}, {3.978994819214058*^9, 
  3.9789948358117647`*^9}, {3.9793489792813187`*^9, 
  3.9793489931010923`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9ad9e61c-cea4-41a0-a521-\
e599c7429130"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Wallpaper\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Spaces \
Attached to Geometry", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978994853671563*^9, 
  3.978994867328792*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"46995593-ff99-4666-bc20-\
b86da41ac79d"],

Cell["\<\
In this notebook, we consider new spaces \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]attached\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] to geometrical points of the manifold, like \
wallpaper. These spaces are gauge fields whose connections represent \
electromagnetism and nuclear forces. These wallpaper spaces have their own \
abstract differential geometries\[LongDash]their own covariant derivatives, \
above and beyond the differential geometry of spacetime itself. But there is \
a big difference:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.9786460283023977`*^9}, {
   3.978646177642584*^9, 3.978646180024088*^9}, {3.978646219196919*^9, 
   3.978646221832672*^9}, {3.978738870146287*^9, 3.978738896485022*^9}, {
   3.9787917205922403`*^9, 3.978791794129325*^9}, 3.978893813352934*^9, {
   3.9789948781292267`*^9, 3.978994896014659*^9}, {3.979349028013843*^9, 
   3.9793490315743237`*^9}, {3.9793491670429087`*^9, 3.979349233412632*^9}, {
   3.980088286163982*^9, 
   3.980088305933013*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c95b6d04-962e-46a0-ac47-\
c90b44aaf33b"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["In gravitation, gauge forces arise FROM the geometry. \
In other theories, gauge forces arise ON the geometry.",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.9786460283023977`*^9}, {
  3.978646177642584*^9, 3.978646180024088*^9}, {3.978646219196919*^9, 
  3.978646221832672*^9}, {3.978738870146287*^9, 3.978738896485022*^9}, {
  3.9787917205922403`*^9, 3.978791794129325*^9}, {3.980088318601659*^9, 
  3.980088324178297*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"eca0e0df-4ca2-4662-b13d-\
06422758055c"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["That\[CloseCurlyQuote]s one reason gravitation \
resists unification with the other forces of Nature.",
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97879180288661*^9, 3.978791833166924*^9}, {
  3.979349244708267*^9, 
  3.979349246497698*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1d99b55f-d1a9-4711-bf92-\
f301849c4261"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "While it is fine to analogize gauge fields as \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]wallpaper,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] the rigorous \
mathematical machinery for this is ",
 StyleBox["fibre bundles",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Appendix 2)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.97864603904847*^9}, {
  3.978646193604847*^9, 3.9786462612918663`*^9}, {3.978738915564204*^9, 
  3.978738919198637*^9}, {3.978791842137179*^9, 3.978791845890905*^9}, {
  3.978893845870328*^9, 3.978893846684181*^9}, {3.978994931919475*^9, 
  3.978994935611334*^9}, {3.979349259091619*^9, 
  3.979349259323943*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"09d42c70-f660-41d6-91eb-\
a15c4faa3028"],

Cell["\<\
The objective of this notebook is to apply \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] \
to these wallpaper gauge fields, encoding transformation laws, invariants, \
and conserved quantities with the same rigor we applied to GR.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978645943294868*^9, 3.978646049988058*^9}, {
  3.9786462670246687`*^9, 3.9786462749793463`*^9}, {3.978646305201108*^9, 
  3.978646320622986*^9}, {3.9787918538270893`*^9, 3.978791855215496*^9}, {
  3.9789949416195*^9, 
  3.978994944574287*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e45636ff-3d1e-4a21-ac6b-\
fcb178545af0"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["A New CD", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978646468171488*^9, 
  3.978646472312533*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c8c2732a-482b-40dd-ad69-\
34c9e0e28e1c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This new overload of CD can compute connections for Abelian (commutative) \
gauges like our scalar phase example. These connections arise on ",
 StyleBox["sections of the principal bundle",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of Appendix 2. We\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll get to connections for non-Abelian \
gauges like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"U", "(", "1", ")"}], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    RowBox[{"SU", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4aa7d432-3705-4021-b822-69ca30d2c149"],
 " in future notebooks."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795270483778*^9, 3.978795277854451*^9}, {
  3.978795415257291*^9, 3.9787954500045643`*^9}, {3.978821069299505*^9, 
  3.978821143212737*^9}, {3.978821224035911*^9, 3.978821242453227*^9}, {
  3.978893877885006*^9, 3.9788939047268047`*^9}, {3.979349284780232*^9, 
  3.9793493096019793`*^9}, {3.9793493397252274`*^9, 3.979349346486093*^9}, {
  3.980088358906061*^9, 
  3.980088362877892*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9e34077f-ed2e-4587-87ba-\
5f5fa8adeb8f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gauge Covariant Derivative", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795468371107*^9, 
  3.978795488321023*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"94acbd51-3b62-4f9c-a4df-\
f9e4ff0aa53d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Inputs", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795503910904*^9, 
  3.9787955045961237`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ef67580c-d7d0-4644-b9c2-\
f49bb71314c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["expr", "Input"],
 ": The field being differentiated, scalar or tensor"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795528199066*^9, 
  3.978795548423512*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"85859702-2d3f-440a-9c1c-\
5c2d0a618c56"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["var", "Input"],
 ": the coordinate function, e.g., ",
 StyleBox["x[\[ScriptCapitalU][\[Mu]]]", "Input"],
 ", the differentiation variable"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97879555492418*^9, 3.978795614319105*^9}, {
  3.97879576904465*^9, 
  3.978795773539029*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0ebc50f6-8428-4da3-99aa-\
009f03b3365b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["q", "Input"],
 ": the coupling constant or \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]charge\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978795636372712*^9, 
  3.978795645409*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"77fc3235-4095-4d8d-96a1-e8b030336e52"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A", "Input"],
 ": the gauge-field connection symbol. We keep \[CapitalGamma] implicitly as \
the spacetime connection for all theories"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9787956548435926`*^9, 3.9787956871354723`*^9}, {
  3.9789949968930073`*^9, 
  3.978995008129044*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"04154e59-9bc7-4076-b83d-\
31acad96ae89"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
    RowBox[{"expr_", ",", "var_", ",", "q_", ",", "A_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"gravitationalPart", ",", "gaugeCorrection", ",", "idx"}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", 
      RowBox[{
      "Calculate", " ", "the", " ", "coordinate", " ", "Covariant", " ", 
       "Derivative", " ", "via", " ", "existing", " ", "CD", " ", 
       RowBox[{"overloads", "."}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", 
      RowBox[{"Handle", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"+", " ", "Christoffels"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"if", " ", "expr", " ", "is", " ", "a", " ", "tensor"}], 
        ")"}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"If", " ", "expr", " ", "is", " ", "a", " ", "scalar"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"just", " ", "return", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "."}]}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"gravitationalPart", "=", 
       RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
        RowBox[{"expr", ",", "var"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"(*", 
       RowBox[{
       "Extract", " ", "the", " ", "index", " ", "from", " ", "the", " ", 
        "differentiation", " ", 
        RowBox[{"variable", "."}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"(*", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"var", " ", "is", " ", "some", " ", 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
        RowBox[{"we", " ", "need", " ", "\[Mu]"}]}], "*)"}], 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"idx", "=", 
       RowBox[{"var", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      
      RowBox[{"(*", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Construct", " ", "the", " ", "Gauge", " ", "Correction"}], ",",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{"e", ".", "g", "."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "i"}], " ", "q", " ", 
         SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"], " ", "*", " ", "expr"}]}], "*)"}], 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"(*", 
       RowBox[{"Note", ":", " ", 
        RowBox[{"This", " ", "A", " ", "has", " ", "a", " ", "DOWN", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", "Covariant", ")"}], " ", "index", " ", "matching", " ", 
         "the", " ", "derivative"}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"gaugeCorrection", "=", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], "*", "q", "*", 
        RowBox[{"A", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "idx", "]"}], "]"}], "*", 
        "expr"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"(*", "Combine", "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"gravitationalPart", "+", "gaugeCorrection"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978646744556492*^9, 3.978646885622224*^9}, 
   3.978724934490802*^9, {3.978795290664665*^9, 3.9787954073020678`*^9}, 
   3.9787954931896*^9, {3.9787956971832857`*^9, 3.978795753281424*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3de2c0a4-4890-4dcd-8310-578ba58e364c"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Electrodynamics Demos", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978700005346057*^9, 3.9787000089781*^9}, {
   3.9787963301955833`*^9, 3.9787963317746277`*^9}, 3.9788004955698223`*^9, 
   3.978821216010556*^9},ExpressionUUID->"2c02b0be-4c78-4b2a-a1b3-\
4a70d6e26bf1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Covariance of the Covariant Derivative", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823576434066*^9, 3.978823591975399*^9}, {
  3.9788236656529293`*^9, 3.978823667365944*^9}, {3.9788607083047037`*^9, 
  3.978860710361669*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"26cab6eb-fabb-4147-9085-\
2e72df92e4fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Forces as Gauge Connections,\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] we subjected the following expression to a 1D \
(Abelian) gauge transformation in a manual calculation. \
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s automate that calculation, now including a specific \
charge, ",
 StyleBox["q",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978820844121111*^9, 3.97882093662414*^9}, {
  3.978821545485203*^9, 3.978821615299986*^9}, {3.978822440304517*^9, 
  3.978822451496654*^9}, {3.97889393859801*^9, 3.9788939593450127`*^9}, {
  3.978995036342866*^9, 3.97899503858642*^9}, {3.9793493785568047`*^9, 
  3.979349410480792*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"db673d5e-f1b1-4938-a6c8-\
a394f4250e7e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"(", 
  RowBox[{"cde", "=", 
   RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "q", ",", 
     "A"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978646926181177*^9, 3.978646943909356*^9}, {
   3.97864698544555*^9, 3.97864700656507*^9}, 3.97880072568736*^9, {
   3.978818102147591*^9, 3.978818102997529*^9}, {3.978820978904854*^9, 
   3.978820983247849*^9}, 3.978821610399053*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e8d9c61f-9eb0-4945-ad72-568d5242b5c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], " ", "q", " ", "\[Psi]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"A", 
     SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.979348779693609*^9, 3.980088432775975*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[9]=",ExpressionUUID->"923deb81-fa9b-4349-9f54-1523fecdea72"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Starting with the gauge transformations", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978820911086568*^9, 3.978820944821334*^9}, {
   3.978822642442547*^9, 3.9788226595359287`*^9}, {3.9789950515919724`*^9, 
   3.978995052535986*^9}, 
   3.979349421152651*^9},ExpressionUUID->"bfcbf30b-9a8f-4a6b-b946-\
5c4170da5fd0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{
       "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], "\[Psi]", "    ", "and", "    ", 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox["A", "_"], 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[CapitalLambda]", " "}]}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978637538672182*^9, 3.97863778411996*^9}, {
   3.9786379712287197`*^9, 3.9786379796646557`*^9}, {3.978821290744693*^9, 
   3.978821330476513*^9}, {3.978822473550243*^9, 3.978822480144888*^9}, {
   3.978822548622191*^9, 3.978822571486229*^9}, 3.978822679099642*^9, {
   3.978822842709276*^9, 3.978822852781521*^9}, {3.979349441948009*^9, 
   3.979349443572904*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bcfea902-d337-4bda-b9ad-\
532a59a7d4c0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gaugeTransforms", "=", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "->", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[ImaginaryI]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
        "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], "\[Psi]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], "]"}], ":>", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"A", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"Partials", "[", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"x", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
       "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978821001702631*^9, 3.978821044361678*^9}, {
   3.978821351660639*^9, 3.9788214177368813`*^9}, {3.978821448541462*^9, 
   3.97882146930516*^9}, {3.978821639276532*^9, 3.978821662429945*^9}, {
   3.978822191621005*^9, 3.9788221929215384`*^9}, 3.978822231151826*^9, {
   3.978823334810932*^9, 3.978823335460462*^9}, 3.978825160269917*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"727a63da-aa90-45dd-adc5-0ffe24da003b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "q", " ", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], " ", 
     "\[Psi]"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"A", 
     SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]_"]}], "\[RuleDelayed]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], "+", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
      RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.97934877969645*^9, 3.980088441958417*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[10]=",ExpressionUUID->"2db2c474-59de-409f-b908-b9a81bd22697"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["prove that the covariant derivative", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978822728959449*^9, 3.978822748830817*^9}, {
  3.978822863916007*^9, 
  3.978822865933402*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"50c162a4-95b1-4c2d-9f84-\
dcfd4b83f679"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "\[Congruent]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox["A", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786435032056303`*^9, 3.978643606837364*^9}, {
  3.978822966772187*^9, 
  3.97882296838054*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7eeea367-8db9-4bb8-83e0-\
0b1addaa1107"],

Cell["transforms exactly the same way as \[Psi]", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978822755950194*^9, 3.9788227570842133`*^9}, {
  3.978822823242772*^9, 
  3.978822836885271*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"73ecf68b-5a23-4059-bef3-\
42897e2d257f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], 
    OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{
      "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
       "\[CapitalLambda]"}]}]], 
    SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9786436192725773`*^9, 3.9786437727905197`*^9}, {
  3.978643806573044*^9, 3.978643946308076*^9}, {3.978644002327197*^9, 
  3.978644220022155*^9}, {3.978644291740561*^9, 3.9786443538434763`*^9}, {
  3.978644388511799*^9, 3.978644510127365*^9}, {3.978822775213642*^9, 
  3.978822798371068*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"19bf54b0-a557-49f3-bd18-\
9d2c3b9dbd1d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We just need one rule for the charge constant (assumes, but does not prove, \
Noether!). Everything else is already in the toolkit\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox["differentiationRules", "Input"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978822882032498*^9, 3.9788229273306627`*^9}, {
  3.978823009564211*^9, 3.978823010008813*^9}, {3.9793494700351887`*^9, 
  3.979349481993554*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"63449289-cd0b-41a0-9449-\
cf2944636b07"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"constantRules", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Partials", "[", 
     RowBox[{"q", ",", 
      RowBox[{"x", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ",
     ":>", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788220405709257`*^9, 3.9788220914844437`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[11]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3f172635-6ee5-4a70-8a61-eb7d220f695e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["q", 
    RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]_"}]], "\[RuleDelayed]", "0"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9793487797032413`*^9, 3.980088448258806*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[11]=",ExpressionUUID->"872bfe79-bc52-47a9-a207-16ab879bfc47"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"transformedCde", "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"cde", " ", "/.", " ", "gaugeTransforms"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
       "differentiationRules"}], "/.", "constantRules"}], ")"}], "//", 
    "Expand"}], "//", "Simplify"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978822102593217*^9, 3.978822112777665*^9}, {
   3.9788222776342163`*^9, 3.9788222792555733`*^9}, {3.9788223692243032`*^9, 
   3.97882240547611*^9}, 3.978823022815748*^9, {3.978823148683112*^9, 
   3.97882316041686*^9}, {3.978823349405294*^9, 3.9788233500015306`*^9}, {
   3.978858170112883*^9, 3.97885818491053*^9}, {3.980088454761086*^9, 
   3.9800884587628*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[12]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b0ec1902-d500-41fa-8f61-43ad9f584e95"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
   RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "q", " ", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], " ", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], " ", "q", " ", "\[Psi]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"A", 
       SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
     RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}], ")"}]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.979348779714642*^9, 3.980088459682919*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[12]=",ExpressionUUID->"db793bad-e4d2-4364-98a8-f58d6fcd39d4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"transformedCde", "===", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[ImaginaryI]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], "cde"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823164654051*^9, 3.97882321873451*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"799324fc-d50c-48e5-bdb5-66f0d5e3b2d1"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.979348779718459*^9, 3.9800884625753727`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[13]=",ExpressionUUID->"01c21c5a-5cdc-4aaf-ace7-8aacc934436f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["QED\[NonBreakingSpace]\[FilledSquare]",
 FontColor->RGBColor[0.14, 0.8, 0.14]]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823232236299*^9, 
  3.978823321181185*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ad7c97ba-d85c-4acc-97c1-\
ef3e695d61dd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Invariance of the Field-Strength Tensor", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823650174912*^9, 3.9788236824567013`*^9}, {
  3.978823896569426*^9, 
  3.978823898592578*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"13a5b2c2-e39a-477b-935b-\
59de3331ef7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The field-strength tensor, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["F", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Nu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a78e8c4-fc08-4a8e-92f9-ce12438ddaad"],
 ", aka ",
 StyleBox["Faraday", "Input"],
 ", is defined as follows"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978824061078446*^9, 
  3.978824098440377*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8f3ecd75-5900-473e-ad73-\
516a0e7c21fe"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"F", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Partials", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Nu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"Partials", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Nu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823709235116*^9, 3.9788237415322437`*^9}, {
  3.978824044627816*^9, 3.978824051061049*^9}, {3.978824190166666*^9, 
  3.9788241975067244`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",ExpressionUUID->"097fd1ac-3cb5-4783-9706-68f9adb7f946"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"-", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], 
     RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]], ")"}]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"A", 
    SubscriptBox["", "\[Nu]"]}], 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.979348779725163*^9, 3.9800885145239277`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[14]=",ExpressionUUID->"42c84c10-0998-4e75-8a4f-382cede17b97"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "usually presented as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], 
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Nu]"}]]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Nu]"], 
     SubscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"e0b7b22c-4b20-45e1-9116-61a69b483886"],
 " to make the indices line up, but our comma notation checks out."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978824215276784*^9, 3.978824267149712*^9}, {
  3.979349527991433*^9, 
  3.979349529193584*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"686c6855-f4f0-4413-b371-\
5d14d6d91172"],

Cell["Now, subject it to the gauge transform:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788242749841127`*^9, 
  3.9788242924403057`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bf1fd84a-386a-4f24-b9a9-\
614cbd977b06"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"F", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}], "/.", " ", 
  "gaugeTransforms"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:=",ExpressionUUID->"41f7d312-8c5c-4141-b7fe-24720dee4831"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"A", 
       SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], "+", 
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
       RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Nu]"]}], "+", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
      RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]]}], ")"}], 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.979348779730495*^9, 3.9800885187822733`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[15]=",ExpressionUUID->"16a209b6-8fc1-4a3f-9ef5-bdf1ccd50160"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "See that it doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t change by invoking the toolkit\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox["ExpandDerivatives", "Input"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978824312009261*^9, 
  3.978824333879499*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"91ab7ee2-27ab-479b-9a7a-\
fcd44e4d6e2e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"F", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}], "/.", " ", "gaugeTransforms"}], 
   ")"}], " ", "//", " ", "ExpandDerivatives", " "}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823798335211*^9, 3.9788238192571917`*^9}, 
   3.978823885830079*^9, {3.9800885293613997`*^9, 3.9800885334193583`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3e9266b1-4af3-4050-81a7-4a26104483a3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"-", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"A", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], 
     RowBox[{",", "\[Nu]"}]], ")"}]}], "+", 
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"A", 
    SubscriptBox["", "\[Nu]"]}], 
   RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9793487797371798`*^9, 3.980088534274623*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[16]=",ExpressionUUID->"08506293-6508-4584-b151-f06468c094a3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["QED\[NonBreakingSpace]\[FilledSquare]", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978823232236299*^9, 3.978823321181185*^9}},
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.14, 0.8, 0.14],ExpressionUUID->"e0e8b96a-c1ba-4281-b112-8fab9afc7dd6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Note: Charge Conservation as a Consequence", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978824417541904*^9, 
  3.978824442338882*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2096586f-c18f-4206-96a3-\
083d7a520f51"],

Cell["\<\
By proving that the covariant derivative transforms just by a phase factor, \
we proved that physical laws built from these derivatives remain invariant \
(unchanged) under gauge transformations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.978824498584906*^9}, {
  3.978824793647162*^9, 
  3.978824804138522*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3b492fc4-9746-4c7b-bbe3-\
24412597a077"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the Lagrangian, phase factors in terms like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox["\[Psi]", "_"], 
     SubscriptBox["D", "\[Mu]"], "\[Psi]"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"3f39fa4f-ea97-4bac-9f03-d117e7518abe"],
 " cancel like this (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{
     "i", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], 
    "*", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "i"}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", "q", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      "\[CapitalLambda]"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2021a6dd-cac1-47c4-baf3-2ac2eaafb0a8"],
 "), showing that our theory has a continuous-in-\[CapitalLambda] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2116f244-5f11-4b19-8032-0415b94708e9"],
 " local (new values of \[CapitalLambda] at every point) symmetry \
(invariance). The symmetry is Abelian because the multiplication of phase \
factors is commutative."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.978824642047434*^9}, {
  3.978824843512475*^9, 3.978824866239888*^9}, {3.978995133679728*^9, 
  3.978995148799527*^9}, {3.980088567197814*^9, 
  3.98008865897119*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"10affd0a-26b4-4de8-9414-\
7f0877557db1"],

Cell["\<\
According to Noether\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Theorem, every continuous symmetry \
(local or not, Abelian or not) implies a conservation law. Leaving \
derivations, which require Lagrangians, to future notebooks, here are the \
pertinent examples:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.978824657601129*^9}, {
  3.980088670564962*^9, 
  3.980088777077443*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"68c0c2a0-1b5d-45cf-9efe-\
d9ad1c9d79e6"],

Cell["time-translation symmetry \[DoubleLongRightArrow] conservation of \
energy", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.978824660443276*^9}, {
  3.9788246931582336`*^9, 
  3.9788247246785107`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1818a92a-ac0c-4215-97aa-\
778ebbffd45b"],

Cell["spatial translation symmetry \[DoubleLongRightArrow] conservation of \
momentum", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.9788246636498423`*^9}, {
  3.978824697325098*^9, 3.978824697877668*^9}, {3.9788247314028273`*^9, 
  3.9788247475931168`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6d3a0f86-db22-4d7c-a644-\
f66a735c0cce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0794a4d9-60d2-4afd-92c2-25f9c9468256"],
 " phase symmetry \[DoubleLongRightArrow] conservation of electric charge"
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788244690128193`*^9, 3.97882470049264*^9}, {
  3.9788247519693537`*^9, 
  3.978824763905596*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"24030461-d0a4-4602-925d-\
c4b1213ef2fb"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Charged Vector Boson Covariance Demo", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9787963383682137`*^9, 3.97879634402703*^9}, {
  3.9788180610060997`*^9, 3.978818067081018*^9}, {3.978825674286153*^9, 
  3.978825699794757*^9}, {3.9788558949345093`*^9, 3.978855894989732*^9}, {
  3.978894667100854*^9, 
  3.978894674216569*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8ac3c528-684d-4beb-ab6b-\
4d1874e0ecab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this demo, we differentiate a charged contravariant vector field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Alpha]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"f7f0a410-0771-455e-95cd-d2e0beef34aa"],
 ", coupled to a neutral field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["Z", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "88ad74ed-b111-4fd8-8cc1-ea31161220e0"],
 " by a scalar hypercharge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["g", "W"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "35d7e3d8-7d42-4838-af7e-052c105ae946"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978894091805274*^9, 3.978894204401751*^9}, {
   3.978894566901813*^9, 3.978894598550589*^9}, {3.978894686707038*^9, 
   3.97889487071537*^9}, {3.978894993424843*^9, 3.978895115120289*^9}, {
   3.978895240365799*^9, 3.9788953047976427`*^9}, {3.97889562488491*^9, 
   3.978895643192864*^9}, {3.979349638268381*^9, 3.979349667320402*^9}, 
   3.9800887943598413`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"3e82e008-b30a-48eb-b50d-\
9725d5f00357"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["Z", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b9bdd90d-1024-42f0-b7a7-92469cea0f56"],
 " acts like a vector phase correction in the non-geometric gauge covariant \
derivative. In addition to this non-geometric phase correction, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Alpha]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"8e627cd2-eb89-4da5-b64e-31baca5053cf"],
 " generates a geometrical correction proportional to \[CapitalGamma], as \
with the geometrical covariant derivative of any tensor. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978894091805274*^9, 3.978894204401751*^9}, {
  3.978894566901813*^9, 3.978894598550589*^9}, {3.978894686707038*^9, 
  3.97889487071537*^9}, {3.978894993424843*^9, 3.978895115120289*^9}, {
  3.978895240365799*^9, 3.9788953047976427`*^9}, {3.97889562488491*^9, 
  3.978895643192864*^9}, {3.979349638268381*^9, 3.979349667320402*^9}, {
  3.9800888063914757`*^9, 
  3.9800888075971737`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0430dbe3-94e7-4daa-b442-\
4cdca8f30f5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We did not need a geometrical correction in electrodynamics because we were \
differentiating a scalar field \[Psi]. Its geometrical covariant derivative \
is exactly equal to its ordinary partial derivative\[LongDash]the twisting \
and turning of spacetime does not change a scalar value. We do not need here \
a geometrical correction for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["Z", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6a30bdca-6b56-4b64-bdb2-743c8adbd262"],
 " because it is not the subject of differentiation here."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978894091805274*^9, 3.978894204401751*^9}, {
  3.978894566901813*^9, 3.978894598550589*^9}, {3.978894686707038*^9, 
  3.97889487071537*^9}, {3.978894993424843*^9, 3.978895075941264*^9}, {
  3.978895212941428*^9, 3.9788952291789*^9}, {3.978895665418445*^9, 
  3.9788957057588253`*^9}, {3.9789952229117727`*^9, 
  3.978995230931829*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dc1ab1e8-3b5f-4225-8398-\
4f2541e96ce4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This expression occurs in the electroweak, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f85baaa9-ed5a-48e3-b2d2-4c1b5563da70"],
 " sector, an Abelian sector (multiple phase operations commute), of the \
Standard Model of Particle Physics. In future notebooks, we will cover \
non-Abelian symmetries like those of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"U", "(", "1", ")"}], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    RowBox[{"SU", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9bfab423-1f01-4181-be65-d2255453aa57"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978894091805274*^9, 3.978894204401751*^9}, {
  3.978894566901813*^9, 3.978894598550589*^9}, {3.978894686707038*^9, 
  3.978894970834722*^9}, {3.9788955765565453`*^9, 3.978895598917972*^9}, {
  3.97899526216114*^9, 
  3.978995271732646*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b682fd5b-0364-4eb8-99de-\
28a25c31d3c4"],

Cell["We proceed just as above", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788249780669603`*^9, 
  3.978824986166164*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f028ebea-692c-482c-9daa-\
62ea02d7489e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"wsd", "=", 
    RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"W", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "gW", ",",
       "Z"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "//", "TensorForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978646926181177*^9, 3.978646944946294*^9}, {
   3.9786470457728977`*^9, 3.978647062184148*^9}, {3.9788243635656977`*^9, 
   3.978824398969141*^9}, 3.978824990560746*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[17]:=",ExpressionUUID->"67be8f28-c827-4885-9074-9540eca97413"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"W", 
     SuperscriptBox["", "\[Alpha]"]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]], "-", 
   RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "gW", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"W", 
      SuperscriptBox["", "\[Alpha]"]}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"Z", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"W", 
      SuperscriptBox["", "\[Lambda]"]}], ")"}], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Lambda]"}], "\[Alpha]"]}]}],
  HoldForm]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.979348779740891*^9, 3.98008885347744*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[17]=",ExpressionUUID->"4a5b300c-e2e1-4c46-bc29-89433e84232c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mixedGaugeTransforms", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"W", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Alpha]_", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ":>", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[ImaginaryI]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "gW", " ", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], 
      "*", 
      RowBox[{"W", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
    "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Z", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ":>", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Z", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Partials", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"x", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
       "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9788250296307173`*^9, 3.9788251409065733`*^9}, {
  3.97882518727766*^9, 3.978825266663143*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[18]:=",ExpressionUUID->"87e77b04-886b-4005-9b7f-8bcbdf3df423"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"W", 
     SuperscriptBox["", "\[Alpha]_"]}], "\[RuleDelayed]", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "gW", " ", "\[CapitalLambda]"}]], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"W", 
       SuperscriptBox["", "\[Alpha]"]}], ")"}]}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Z", 
     SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]_"]}], "\[RuleDelayed]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Z", 
      SubscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], "+", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
      RowBox[{",", "\[Mu]"}]]}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.979348779747698*^9, 3.980088855779813*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[18]=",ExpressionUUID->"fb9f0dbe-5fb6-499d-82ad-22a18fbb1f7e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"transformedWsd", "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"wsd", "/.", "mixedGaugeTransforms"}], "//.", 
       "differentiationRules"}], "/.", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Partials", "[", 
